---
import SiteLayout from "../components/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy · 3Dweather" path="/privacy" description="What 3Dweather stores about you: nearly nothing.">
  <article class="article">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">No accounts, no cookies, no analytics, no advertising.</p>
    <h2>In your browser</h2>
    <p>The site remembers a few choices in your browser's own storage: metres or feet, and whether you have seen
      the opening animation this visit. They never leave your device; clear your browser's site data to remove them.</p>
    <h2>Your location</h2>
    <p>"Tides near you" asks your browser for your position only when you press the button. The nearest places
      are worked out on your device; your position is not sent to us or anyone else.</p>
    <h2>Other services</h2>
    <p>Pages and data are served by Cloudflare, which keeps standard request logs. The finder map loads map tiles
      from OpenStreetMap's servers, which see your IP address under the
      <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy">OpenStreetMap Foundation privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
